   178	**N10. The Bergman frame lemma, measured (section I).** Spectrum of `(N/pi)S_V` on `ker H_N` for the
   179	conic, `S_V = int_V |e_p><e_p| dvol_V` on a 900x96 Gauss-Legendre grid; Geometry step 2 (the
   180	argument's only unproved leaf) says these are asymptotically flat at 1. Min / max / mean on
   181	`ker H_N`, and max on `I_N`: `N=6`: 0.890019 / 1.032096 / 0.923077 / 7.2e-16; `N=10`: 0.930690 /
   182	1.038218 / 0.952381 / 1.2e-15; `N=14`: 0.949404 / 1.035624 / 0.965517 / 1.0e-15; `N=18`: 0.960160 /
   183	1.032098 / 0.972973 / 9.7e-16. The mean is exactly `2N/(2N+1) = vol(V)N/(pi HF)` (an identity, steps
   184	2.2-2.3); the spread falls as 0.14, 0.11, 0.086, 0.072, i.e. `O(1/N)`; `S_V` annihilates `I_N` to
   185	machine precision, confirming `ran S_V = ker H_N` exactly (C-028).
