   187	## Geometry
   188	
   189	Lamport-hierarchical sketch (L3); leaves cite a D-id, a C-id, or a named script section.
   190	
   191	**ASSUME.** **A1** `I, J` homogeneous radical; `V = V(I)`, `W = V(J)` smooth of dimensions
   192	`k_1, k_2` (D-homogeneous-ideal, D-variety). **A2** `N >= max(reg I, reg J)`
   193	(D-saturation-regularity-stable-range), so `I_N = I(V)_N`, `J_N = I(W)_N`. **A3** the intersection is
   194	**clean**: `Z = V ^ W` smooth of pure dimension `l` and `T_xV ^ T_xW = T_xZ` for every `x in Z`
   195	(transversal is `dim_R(T_xV + T_xW) = 2n`, i.e. `l = k_1+k_2-n`; excess-but-clean is
   196	`l > k_1+k_2-n`; tangency violates A3). **A4** the metric convention above, with
   197	`theta_i(x)` the principal angles between `T_xV (-) T_xZ` and `T_xW (-) T_xZ`,
   198	`J(x) = prod_i sin^2 theta_i(x)`.
   199	
   200	**PROVE.** `Tr(P_I P_J) = (N/pi)^l int_Z J(x)^{-1} dvol_Z(x) . (1 + O(1/N))`.
   201	
   202	1. `P_I` projects onto `H_V := span{e_p : p in V}`.
   203	   1.1 `ran P_I = ker H_N = (I_N)^perp` [D-ground-space, D-projectors, D-inverse-system].
   204	   1.2 `(I_N)^perp = (I(V)_N)^perp` [A2].
   205	   1.3 `(I(V)_N)^perp = span{e_p : conj(p) in V}` [C-028, C-026, D-coherent-state]; the conjugation
   206	   is C3 and is immaterial for the real-coefficient examples N1-N10.
   207	2. **(Bergman frame lemma.)** `S_V := int_V |e_p><e_p| dvol_V(p) = (pi/N)^{k_1}(P_I + E_N)`,
   208	   `||E_N|| = O(1/N)`.
   209	   2.1 `ran S_V = H_V` exactly for every `N` [step 1; `S_V >= 0` and `<u|S_V|u> = 0` iff `u` is
   210	   orthogonal to every `e_p`, `p in V`]. Measured to 1e-15 in N10.
   211	   2.2 `Tr S_V = int_V ||e_p||^2 dvol_V = vol(V) = deg V . pi^{k_1}/k_1!` [Wirtinger].
   212	   2.3 `rank S_V = HF_{R/I}(N) = deg V . N^{k_1}/k_1! (1+O(1/N))` [A2, D-hilbert-function].
   213	   2.4 So the *mean* eigenvalue of `(N/pi)^{k_1}S_V` on `H_V` is `1 + O(1/N)`. The lemma is the
   214	   stronger statement that the eigenvalues are asymptotically **flat**, i.e. Tian-Zelditch-Catlin
   215	   Bergman asymptotics for `(V, O(N)|_V)` read in the ambient frame [Tian,
   216	   DOI 10.4310/jdg/1214445039; Zelditch, arXiv:math-ph/0002009]. **LEAF STATUS: the one step this
   217	   lane does not prove** -- a citation plus the spectral measurement N10; everything downstream
   218	   inherits its status.
   219	3. `Tr(P_I P_J) = (N/pi)^{k_1+k_2} Tr(S_V S_W)(1+O(1/N))` [step 2 twice; `P_I, P_J` projectors].
   220	4. `Tr(S_V S_W) = int_V int_W |<e_p,e_q>|^2 = int_V int_W cos^{2N}d(p,q)` [D-coherent-state:
   221	   `<e_p,e_q> = <p,q>^N`; A4].
   222	5. **(Laplace.)** `int_V int_W cos^{2N}d = (pi/N)^{k_1+k_2-l} int_Z J^{-1}dvol_Z (1+O(1/N))`.
   223	   5.1 `cos^{2N}d = exp(-Nd^2(1+O(d^2)))`, concentrating at `d = O(N^{-1/2})` where the correction
   224	   is `O(1/N)`.
   225	   5.2 The zero set of `d` on `V x W` is the diagonal `{(x,x): x in Z}`, real dimension `2l`.
   226	   5.3 In normal coordinates at `x in Z`, with `L = T_xV`, `M = T_xW`, the form `|u-v|^2` on `L x M`
   227	   has kernel exactly `{(e,e): e in T_xZ}` -- this **is** A3 -- and is positive definite on a
   228	   complement of real dimension `dim_R(L+M) = 2(k_1+k_2-l)`.
   229	   5.4 The Gaussian integral over that complement is `(pi/N)^{k_1+k_2-l}` over the Jacobian of
   230	   `(u',v') -> u'-v'` from `(L (-) T_xZ) x (M (-) T_xZ)` onto `(L+M) (-) T_xZ`, which is
   231	   `prod sin theta` over the *real* principal angles; a complex angle occurs twice, giving `J(x)`
   232	   [linear algebra; verified to 8 digits against N1, N2 and the curved cases N5, N6].
   233	6. Combining 3-5: `(N/pi)^{k_1+k_2}(pi/N)^{k_1+k_2-l} = (N/pi)^l`. QED modulo 2.4.
   234	
   235	**Corollary 6a (Hilbert-function identity).** For `J(x) = J` constant on `Z`,
   236	`int_Z J^{-1}dvol_Z = deg(Z)pi^l/(l!J)`, so `Tr(P_I P_J) = HF_{R/(I+J)}(N)/J . (1+O(1/N))`; under A3
   237	the scheme `V ^ W` is reduced, so `I+J` may replace its radical in the stable range.
   238	**Corollary 6b.** Under A1-A4 the growth exponent is exactly `dim(V ^ W)` -- transversal or excess,
   239	provided clean. **Corollary 6c (disjoint).** If `V ^ W = {}`, with `d_0 = d_FS(V,W) > 0` and `S` the
   240	set of closest pairs, the same argument gives `Tr = C N^{dim_C S}cos^{2N}(d_0)(1+o(1))`, hence
   241	`-(1/2N)log Tr = log sec d_0 - dim_C(S)log N/(2N) + O(1/N)`. Clifford pair: `dim_C S = 1` and the
   242	closed form is exact; generic skew pair: `dim_C S = 0` (N4). This is C-167 with its missing
   243	polynomial prefactor and its bias made explicit.
   244	
   245	**What fails without each hypothesis.** Without **A2**, `(I_N)^perp` strictly contains the coherent
   246	span (D-entangled-defect), step 1.3 fails, and the observable also measures irrelevant torsion.
   247	Without **A1** the same, plus multiplicity entering through jets. Without **smoothness**, 5.3 has no
   248	tangent space and the local exponent becomes an invariant of the singularity. Without **A3** the
   249	exponent changes: for smooth curves in `CP^2` meeting at one point with contact order `m` (local
   250	model `d^2 = |u-v|^2 + |gamma|^2|u|^{2m}` in a Fubini-Study normal chart, and
   251	`int_C exp(-N|gamma|^2|u|^{2m})dA = pi Gamma(1+1/m)(N|gamma|^2)^{-1/m}`),
   252	**`Tr(P_I P_J) -> Gamma(1+1/m)|gamma|^{-2/m}N^{1-1/m}`**. Since the intersection multiplicity of two
   253	smooth curves with contact order `m` is `m`, the exponent is `1 - 1/mu`: a non-integer rational fixed
   254	by the multiplicity, not the dimension (N5 measures `m = 2`, `gamma = 1`). **Near-**failure of A3 is
   255	worse than failure: `J -> 0` inflates the constant and the asymptotic regime only begins at
   256	`N ~ mu_cap` (N3, N6).
