   258	## Against the north star
   259	
   260	**1 -- Problem (met).** Same input throughout (D-input-model: sparse generators of `I, J`, `poly(n)`
   261	monomials and coefficient bits, `N` unary). **P0 (native):** estimate `tau_N = Tr(P_I P_J)/M_N` to
   262	additive `eps`. **P1 (dimension):** with A1-A3, `reg <= N`, `Delta_N/alpha_BE >= 1/poly` for both
   263	ideals and `mu_cap <= poly`, decide `dim(V ^ W) >= l` versus `<= l-1`. **P2 (distance):** with
   264	`V ^ W = {}`, estimate `d_FS(V,W)` to additive `eta`. **P3 (integration):** estimate
   265	`vol(V)^{-1}int_V g dvol_V` to additive `eps`. All four are precisely stated; all are promise
   266	problems; the promise list has five entries, two of which (`mu_cap`, cleanness) this lane had to
   267	invent because the seed does not state them.
   268	
   269	**2 -- Classical baseline (failed).** For P1 the baseline is not trace estimation but numerical
   270	algebraic geometry: witness sets and numerical irreducible decomposition [SVW,
   271	DOI 10.1137/S0036142900372549] present `V, W` as witness point sets of sizes `deg V`, `deg W`; the
   272	diagonal homotopy [SVW, DOI 10.1137/S0036142903430463] intersects them in `deg V . deg W` path tracks
   273	and returns the **exact integer** `dim(V ^ W)` with witness points on each component; the trace test
   274	[SVW, DOI 10.1137/S0036142901397101] certifies it; tracking is `poly(n)` per path on average [Lairez,
   275	DOI 10.1007/s10208-016-9319-7; D-condition-number], implemented in HomotopyContinuation.jl
   276	[arXiv:1711.10911]. For P3 the baseline is C-087 (slice with a random linear space -- the points are
   277	Fubini-Study distributed by the kinematic formula -- and average): `O(1/eps^2)` samples of `deg V`
   278	tracks each. For P0 the baseline is Hutch++ [arXiv:2010.09649] on the PSD operator `P_I P_J P_I`
   279	(note `Tr(P_I P_J) = ||P_J P_I||_F^2 >= 0`): `O(1/eps_rel)` matrix-vector products, each two spectral
   280	filters of `O~(M_N s_row alpha_BE/Delta_N)` flops by sparse Krylov; dense rank is not the baseline
   281	(classical memo trap 1). Decisively: `HF_{R/(I+J)}(N)` is a rank of the concatenated Macaulay matrix,
   282	so the exact answer to P1 at level `N` costs one Hilbert-function evaluation, no Groebner basis and
   283	no elimination.
   284	
   285	**3 -- Quantum algorithm (partial, no arm-specific margin).** P0 is a D-dqc1-style-estimate:
   286	maximally mixed state on the weak-composition register (`O(n log N)` qubits), two QSVT spectral
   287	projectors (D-qsvt, D-projectors) at `O~(alpha_BE/Delta_N . log(1/eps'))` block-encoding uses each,
   288	Hadamard test; `O(1/eps)` rounds with amplitude estimation. Total
   289	`O~(poly(n, log N)(alpha_I/Delta_I + alpha_J/Delta_J)/eps)`. Reading an *exponent* needs
   290	`tau_{2N}/tau_N` to relative accuracy `1/4`, so `eps = Theta(tau_N)` and `Omega(1/tau_N)` rounds, and
   291	needs `N >~ mu_cap` (N3): honest bound `O~(poly(n, N, mu_cap, alpha_BE/Delta_N)/tau_N)`. Against the
   292	classical `Omega(M_N)` per filter the margin is exactly `M_N` -- exponential when `N = Theta(n)`, but
   293	it is arm A's margin for `HF/M_N` applied to a concatenated generator list, not a new one. Space
   294	`O(n log N)` qubits versus `M_N` words is not by itself a separation (fact SP-0, PRD D15) and must be
   295	stated as a simultaneous (space, time) claim (D-space-time-pareto).
   296	
   297	**4 -- Dequantization audit (failed).** Low-rank dequantization (Tang; Gilyen-Lloyd-Tang; Chia et
   298	al.) does not apply: `H_N` is sparse and high rank and `P_I` has rank `HF(N)`, a constant fraction of
   299	`M_N` at low codimension (D-hardness-anchors). The live attack is the classical comparator. (i)
   300	Hutch++ is already `O(1/eps)` matvecs for PSD inputs, so amplitude estimation beats naive Hutchinson,
   301	not the stated best classical baseline (`scouting/quantum-primitives.md`, Combinations preamble).
   302	(ii) What remains is the vector length `M_N`, the generic "quantum works in the exponentially large
   303	space" claim. (iii) The seed's selling point, "without forming `I + J`", is void (criterion 2). (iv)
   304	The answer is an exponent, and extracting it needs `eps = Theta(tau_N)`; `tau_N` obeys the campaign's
   305	codimension law (`applications-wide-net.md` caution 1, `rho^codim`, `rho ~ 0.75` at `N = n`), so the
   306	cost is `rho^{-codim(V^W)}`. (v) One nominal margin survives: for `V, W` complete intersections of
   307	quadrics with `codim(V^W) = c`, the classical witness route needs `deg V . deg W = 2^c` path tracks
   308	while the quantum estimator needs `rho^{-c} ~ 1.33^c` amplitude-estimation rounds -- an exponential
   309	with a smaller base. It is fragile: it ignores `mu_cap` and `alpha_BE/Delta_N`, and the classical
   310	route returns points and a certificate where the quantum route returns a real number from which an
   311	integer must be inferred.
   312	
   313	**5 -- Heuristic hardware (met).** With `rho_I = P_I/HF_I`, `rho_J = P_J/HF_J`, a **bosonic SWAP
   314	test** -- mode-wise 50:50 beam splitters between the two `(n+1)`-mode registers, then photon-number
   315	parity in the difference modes, i.e. many-mode Hong-Ou-Mandel interference -- measures
   316	`Tr(rho_I rho_J) = Tr(P_I P_J)/(HF_I HF_J)` with `O(1/eps^2)` shots, no postselection and no
   317	non-Gaussian element. (a) **Linear `V, W`:** `rho_I` is `N` photons maximally mixed over the
   318	symmetric subspace of a `(k+1)`-mode subspace, reachable with a passive interferometer and a
   319	phase-randomised source; the smallest instance is `n = 2`, `N = 1`, two lines in `P^2` at angle `t`,
   320	measuring `(1+cos^2 t)/4` -- an interferometric measurement of the angle between two projective
   321	lines, classically trivial. (b) **The conic:** `ker H_N` for `z_0z_1 - z_2^2` is the `2N+1`-fold
   322	degenerate ferromagnetic ground manifold of the Law-Pu-Bigelow spin-mixing Hamiltonian (C-024,
   323	D-spin-mixing-hamiltonian, DOI 10.1103/PhysRevLett.81.5257); two such condensates in relatively
   324	rotated bases, interfered, measure `Tr(P_I P_J)/(2N+1)^2` for two conics, whose limit N6 predicts
   325	exactly. A genuine analogue measurement of a Bezout-type constant times an angle factor -- and not a
   326	speedup, three modes being fixed `n` and therefore classically polynomial by C-099 [arXiv:2211.16998,
   327	DOI 10.22331/q-2023-11-28-1189].
   328	
   329	**Verdict 2/5.** Report the arm as producing three theorems (the clean-intersection asymptotic with
   330	its explicit constant, the tangency exponent `1 - 1/mu`, and `Tr = HF_{R/(I+J)}/J`) plus four
   331	negative algorithmic results, then close it as a speedup route unless PRD §7 Q4 is answered in favour
   332	of dictionary theorems.
