   393	## Proposed definitions
   394	
   395	MERGE PROPOSAL (`definitions/definitions.md`); all verified in the lane script.
   396	
   397	**D-intersection-overlap.** `T_N(I,J) := Tr(P_{0,N}^{(I)}P_{0,N}^{(J)})`, `P_{0,N}` the projector
   398	onto `ker H_N` (D-projectors), i.e. the Bergman projector of D-bergman-projector; equivalently
   399	`||B_I^dag B_J||_F^2` for orthonormal ground-space bases, and `= Tr(P_I P_J P_I) >= 0`. Three
   400	normalisations, all in use: `tau_N = T_N/M_N` (the D-dqc1-style-estimate quantity),
   401	`T_N/sqrt(HF_I HF_J)`, `T_N/(HF_I HF_J) = Tr(rho_I rho_J)` (what a two-copy SWAP test measures).
   402	Source: seed §5.7 L159, Conjecture 8.10(a); this lane. Pitfalls: it is **not**
   403	`Tr(P_{I_N}P_{J_N}) = M_N - HF_I - HF_J + T_N = Theta(M_N)`; the three normalisations differ by
   404	factors exponential in codimension, so a signal-size statement must say which.
   405	
   406	**D-clean-intersection.** Smooth `V, W` in `CP^n` intersect cleanly along `Z = V ^ W` if `Z` is
   407	smooth of pure dimension and `T_xV ^ T_xW = T_xZ` for every `x in Z` (Bott). Transversal implies
   408	clean; clean also covers **excess** intersection (`dim Z > k_1+k_2-n`); tangential contact is exactly
   409	the failure. Source: this lane, Geometry A3. Pitfalls: this, not transversality, is the hypothesis
   410	every intersection-overlap asymptotic needs; C-166's "transversal" is strictly stronger and misses the
   411	excess case, the only case in which the observable answers a question Krull does not.
   412	
   413	**D-intersection-angle-condition-number.** For a clean intersection,
   414	`J(x) = prod_i sin^2 theta_i(x)` over the principal angles between `T_xV (-) T_xZ` and
   415	`T_xW (-) T_xZ`, and `mu_cap(V,W) := sup_{x in Z}J(x)^{-1} in [1, infinity]`; `mu_cap = 1` iff the
   416	tangent spaces meet orthogonally modulo `T_xZ`, `= infinity` iff the intersection is not clean.
   417	Source: this lane, Geometry 5.4. Pitfalls: arm C's condition number, the analogue of
   418	D-condition-number for the observable; the asymptotic regime begins only at `N ~ mu_cap`, so
   419	`mu_cap` belongs in every promise and every cost bound.
   420	
   421	**D-bergman-frame-operator.** `S_V^{(N)} := int_V |e_p><e_p| dvol_V(p)` on `R_N` for smooth `V` of
   422	dimension `k` with the induced Fubini-Study volume. Exactly `ran S_V = (I(V)_N)^perp` (C-028);
   423	asymptotically `S_V^{(N)} = (pi/N)^k(P_I + O(1/N))` [Tian, DOI 10.4310/jdg/1214445039; Zelditch,
   424	arXiv:math-ph/0002009]. Source: this lane, Geometry step 2. Pitfalls: the trace and rank identities
   425	are elementary and exact; the flatness of the spectrum is the cited, unproved part, and every
   426	asymptotic constant in arm C rests on it.
   427	
   428	**D-normalised-toeplitz-operator.** Amendment to D-toeplitz-operator: for `g(z, conj z)` of bidegree
   429	`(r,r)` the level-`N` Toeplitz operator must carry the degree normalisation
   430	`T_g^{(N)} = ((N-r)!/N!)P_0 :g(a^dag,a): P_0`, whose Berezin symbol is exactly `g(p, conj p)` for
   431	every `N`. Without it `Tr(P_0 T_g)/HF(N)` diverges like `N^r` and C-168 is dimensionally false as
   432	stated. Examples: `r=1`, `g = |z_2|^2`, `T_g = n_2/N`; `r=2`, `g = |z_2|^4`,
