   272	diagonal homotopy [SVW, DOI 10.1137/S0036142903430463] intersects them in `deg V . deg W` path tracks
   273	and returns the **exact integer** `dim(V ^ W)` with witness points on each component; the trace test
   274	[SVW, DOI 10.1137/S0036142901397101] certifies it; tracking is `poly(n)` per path on average [Lairez,
   275	DOI 10.1007/s10208-016-9319-7; D-condition-number], implemented in HomotopyContinuation.jl
   276	[arXiv:1711.10911]. For P3 the baseline is C-087 (slice with a random linear space -- the points are
   277	Fubini-Study distributed by the kinematic formula -- and average): `O(1/eps^2)` samples of `deg V`
   278	tracks each. For P0 the baseline is Hutch++ [arXiv:2010.09649] on the PSD operator `P_I P_J P_I`
   279	(note `Tr(P_I P_J) = ||P_J P_I||_F^2 >= 0`): `O(1/eps_rel)` matrix-vector products, each two spectral
   280	filters of `O~(M_N s_row alpha_BE/Delta_N)` flops by sparse Krylov; dense rank is not the baseline
   281	(classical memo trap 1). Decisively: `HF_{R/(I+J)}(N)` is a rank of the concatenated Macaulay matrix,
   282	so the exact answer to P1 at level `N` costs one Hilbert-function evaluation, no Groebner basis and
   283	no elimination.
