   299	`M_N` at low codimension (D-hardness-anchors). The live attack is the classical comparator. (i)
   300	Hutch++ is already `O(1/eps)` matvecs for PSD inputs, so amplitude estimation beats naive Hutchinson,
   301	not the stated best classical baseline (`scouting/quantum-primitives.md`, Combinations preamble).
   302	(ii) What remains is the vector length `M_N`, the generic "quantum works in the exponentially large
   303	space" claim. (iii) The seed's selling point, "without forming `I + J`", is void (criterion 2). (iv)
   304	The answer is an exponent, and extracting it needs `eps = Theta(tau_N)`; `tau_N` obeys the campaign's
   305	codimension law (`applications-wide-net.md` caution 1, `rho^codim`, `rho ~ 0.75` at `N = n`), so the
   306	cost is `rho^{-codim(V^W)}`. (v) One nominal margin survives: for `V, W` complete intersections of
   307	quadrics with `codim(V^W) = c`, the classical witness route needs `deg V . deg W = 2^c` path tracks
   308	while the quantum estimator needs `rho^{-c} ~ 1.33^c` amplitude-estimation rounds -- an exponential
   309	with a smaller base. It is fragile: it ignores `mu_cap` and `alpha_BE/Delta_N`, and the classical
   310	route returns points and a certificate where the quantum route returns a real number from which an
   311	integer must be inferred.
