   313	**5 -- Heuristic hardware (met).** With `rho_I = P_I/HF_I`, `rho_J = P_J/HF_J`, a **bosonic SWAP
   314	test** -- mode-wise 50:50 beam splitters between the two `(n+1)`-mode registers, then photon-number
   315	parity in the difference modes, i.e. many-mode Hong-Ou-Mandel interference -- measures
   316	`Tr(rho_I rho_J) = Tr(P_I P_J)/(HF_I HF_J)` with `O(1/eps^2)` shots, no postselection and no
   317	non-Gaussian element. (a) **Linear `V, W`:** `rho_I` is `N` photons maximally mixed over the
   318	symmetric subspace of a `(k+1)`-mode subspace, reachable with a passive interferometer and a
   319	phase-randomised source; the smallest instance is `n = 2`, `N = 1`, two lines in `P^2` at angle `t`,
   320	measuring `(1+cos^2 t)/4` -- an interferometric measurement of the angle between two projective
   321	lines, classically trivial. (b) **The conic:** `ker H_N` for `z_0z_1 - z_2^2` is the `2N+1`-fold
   322	degenerate ferromagnetic ground manifold of the Law-Pu-Bigelow spin-mixing Hamiltonian (C-024,
   323	D-spin-mixing-hamiltonian, DOI 10.1103/PhysRevLett.81.5257); two such condensates in relatively
   324	rotated bases, interfered, measure `Tr(P_I P_J)/(2N+1)^2` for two conics, whose limit N6 predicts
   325	exactly. A genuine analogue measurement of a Bezout-type constant times an angle factor -- and not a
   326	speedup, three modes being fixed `n` and therefore classically polynomial by C-099 [arXiv:2211.16998,
   327	DOI 10.22331/q-2023-11-28-1189].
