   110	not dense SDP); normalised Hermite signature with a succinct oracle (2/5); real-radical
   111	inverse system from a truncated moment state (2/5); positive toric fibre Hamiltonians (2/5
   112	speedup, 4/5 hardware, but stoquastic); totally real Boolean varieties (2/5, Grover-limited).
   113	Nine claim rows C-255..C-263 and seven D-entries merged verbatim. Two corrections to arm R:
   114	the seed ground energy is NOT the Lasserre/DPS value without maximal-symmetry and localizing
   115	constraints (C-261 (C-NEW-RV-R1-NONEQUIVALENCE)), and the "250 GB versus 300 qubits" space
   116	statement in bet R1 compares against dense SDP when the seed matrix admits O(B_3)-space
   117	Lanczos (K-RV8/9); R1 must be reframed as a spectral-hierarchy comparison.
   118	
   119	**Arm R, space direction (D13).** `scouting/robotics-space.md` (Opus, 1363 lines).
   120	Governing fact SP-0: BQSPACE(s) is contained in DSPACE(s^2) and DTIME(2^O(s)) (Watrous 2003
   121	composed with Borodin–Cook–Pippenger 1983; the log-space case is quoted verbatim by
   122	Fefferman–Remscrim). Consequences: with a re-readable input, a pure quantum space advantage
   123	can never exceed a quadratic gap in the space exponent; "n log N qubits versus M_N words" is
   124	not a space separation; at n=100, r=3 the honest classical space for the residual-hierarchy
   125	minimum eigenvalue is about 300 bits, not 250 GB and not 28 MB. What survives is a
   126	SIMULTANEOUS (space, time) claim: quantum poly(n, log N) space with poly time under a
   127	guiding-state promise, versus classical either M_N words or log^2 space with poly(M_N)
   128	time; no classical algorithm with both is known, and none exists unless BQP = BPP provided
   129	the bosonic guided-local-Hamiltonian problem (C-269 (C-NEW-SP-GLH-BOSONIC)) is BQP-hard.
   130	Two survivors: (i) streaming / communication: an UNCONDITIONAL separation, tiny margin,
   131	realisable with one photon in n modes plus phase shifters and one beamsplitter, close
   132	relative already run (DOI 10.1038/s41467-019-12139-z); (ii) succinct-operator (space, time)
   133	Pareto claim, large nominal margin, conditional, and currently missing a robotics family that
   134	provably needs Lasserre order r >= 3. Killer coverage: K5 right for zero-dimensional root
   135	lists, wrong for certification, inconsistent noisy systems, positive-dimensional witness
   136	sets, streaming; K6 right at polynomial space, silent at the s versus s^2 resolution where
   137	every real space claim lives; K-RV8 walls out at r=4..6 (736 MB to 273 GB at n=100); K-RV9
   138	is a treewidth statement that fails for hub-coupled TLS perception. Eleven rows
   139	C-264..C-274 and three definitions merged verbatim.
