   141	Two-copy real-symmetry probe (D14, `scouting/two-copy-real-filter.md`): the STRONG form
   142	is closed. For a real ideal the compressed pairing-state filter on ker H_N x ker H_N has rank
   143	one and top eigenvalue HF/M_N regardless of whether V has any real points; a conjugate pair
   144	|p>^N + |pbar>^N passes with R = 1 although p is complex (C-276, C-278). The filter sees
   145	"real vector in the ground space", not "real point". What survives: the coherent-state
   146	response R = (cos 2t)^{2N} with t the Fubini–Study angle to RP^n (C-277); an exact real-point
   147	COUNT #V_R = Tr(G_hat^{-1} G) from the coherent frame (C-279), inheriting Hermite
   148	conditioning K-RV6; and a one-pair linear-optics-native CERTIFICATE that a supplied product
   149	ground state is a real point (C-280): it verifies, it does not find. Second quantisation:
   150	|Phi_N> is the N-photon sector of the multimode two-mode-squeezed vacuum, so the pairwise Bell
   151	projection is native, at acceptance (n+1)^{-N} pairwise versus 1/M_N collective.
